/-!
# Native words for all F occurrences through a first-class point

The seven labels of each of the 330 candidates are transported from the same
seed by a word in the original max2 generators. A packed table selects a pair
of noncommuting labels for every two distinct candidates. These are data only;
`OccurrenceChecks` checks every edge and separation in the Lean kernel, and
`Occurrences` uses the ambient count to prove exhaustiveness.

The split-tree layout is generated from the retained native ATLAS action data
by `Scratch/J4NamedLocalGeometry/generate_occurrence_witnesses.py`. The seed
words, action conventions and source attribution are those of `SeedIntersection`.
Source: Kleidman--Wilson (1988), Section 2.1, pp.488--489.
-/

